 enum PlayerEnginePriority {
     /// The order a fresh install tries engines in, restricted to the engines
     /// available on this platform.
+    /// Lume GF: KSPlayer first, as up to Lume 3.1 (Lume 3.2 leads with AetherEngine): Lume GF's player work (the
+    /// iPhone Duo's layouts, channel-change timing, the live probe, the enhancer) is KSPlayer's, and with 3.2 every
+    /// device that never ordered its engines quietly lost it (Georgs, 16-17 Nov). A stored order is kept as it is.
     nonisolated static var defaultOrder: [PlayerEngineKind] {
-        [.aetherEngine, .lumeEngine, .ksPlayer, .vlcKit, .avPlayer].filter(\.isAvailable)
+        [.ksPlayer, .vlcKit, .avPlayer, .lumeEngine, .aetherEngine].filter(\.isAvailable)
     }
 
     /// Decode the stored priority into a complete, de-duplicated engine list.
